1	---
2	name: use-uv-tool
3	description: Includes user instructions on how to use UV. Use when using UV tools.
4	disable-model-invocation: false
5	---
6	
7	# uv Best Practices
8	
9	## What is uv?
10	
11	uv is an extremely fast Python package and project manager.
12	
13	## Mandatory Requirements (Must Follow)
14	
15	* For any Python project, deployment using `uv` is mandatory.
16	* You must create a separate virtual development environment for each MCP server project using the commands `uv venv` or `uv sync`.
17	* You must use `uv` to manage Python environments and dependencies. The commands `python` or `pip` are prohibited because they bypass the separate virtual development environment and disrupt the user's local development environment.
18	* Replace the Python and pip commands in the deployment tutorial with the following:
19	  - Running Python scripts: Use `uv run <script>.py`, do not use `python <script>.py`
20	  - Installing dependencies: `uv pip install <package>`, do not use `pip install <package>`
21	
22	---
23	
24	## uv Usage Guide
25	
26	### Running Tools
27	
28	* `uvx` is used to run command-line tools. When used, the tool is installed into a temporary, isolated environment.
29	
30	```bash
31	$ uvx --python 3.10 ruff
32	```
33	
34	* The interface varies significantly between different versions of the mcp package, which can easily lead to interface incompatibility issues when using uvx. If you encounter this problem, please use the smallest available version as the dependency. You can use this command(curl -s https://pypi.org/pypi/<package>/json | jq '.info') to get package dependency information.
35	
36	```bash
37	$ uvx --with mcp[cli]==x.x.x <mcp server> # Version x.x.x is the minimum available version.
38	```
39	
40	**Note**: Executing the `uvx <package>` command will start the server and wait for communication, causing the process to block. This does not necessarily mean the server failed to start. Do not use this method to verify whether the server can start, because even if the server starts normally, it will time out while waiting for input.
41	
42	## Two Methods for Setting Up a uv Project
43	
44	For any project, follow the steps carefully and manage the project using uv.
45	
46	```bash
47	$ uv init # Initialize the project
48	$ uv add <package> # Add a dependency package
49	$ uv sync # Create a virtual environment and install dependencies
50	```
51	
52	Alternatively:
53	
54	```bash
55	$ uv init # Initialize the project
56	$ uv venv # Create a virtual environment
57	$ uv pip install <package> # Install dependencies in the virtual environment
58	```
59	
60	## Environment Setup (Guarantees)
61	
62	- uv has already been deployed to the user’s development environment; simply use it directly.
63	
64	```bash
65	$ which uv
66	{HOME}/.local/bin/uv
67	
68	$ which uvx
69	{HOME}/.local/bin/uvx
70	```
71	
72	* Always navigate to the project directory before running any uv commands.
73	
74	```bash
75	$ cd /path/to/project/dir && uv xxx
76	```

